  "final_text": "I looked these up through the Kibana API using read-only requests and changed nothing.\n\n1. **Panels:** The 'Site health' dashboard has 2 panels, both charts on the web-logs data view: \"Requests over time\" (a line chart) and \"Requests by response code\" (a bar chart).\n2. **Rule name:** The rule is called \"Server errors\". It's the only alert rule in Kibana. It's an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs` that counts responses whose code starts with \"5\" and fires when there are more than 10 in a 5-minute window.\n3. **Interval:** It checks every 1 minute. The 5-minute window is just how far back each check looks, not how often it runs.\n4. **Enabled:** No, the rule is disabled.\n\nPANELS: 2\nRULE_NAME: Server errors\nINTERVAL: 1m\nENABLED: no",
